                    "text": "As Sally, my curiosity lies not only in understanding the implications of surveillance on mental health but also in designing urban spaces that balance security with individual autonomy. By proposing \"Privacy-By-Design Cities: Weaving Individual Autonomy Into the Fabric of Smart Urban Spaces\", my goal is to explore how future cities can adopt a privacy-first approach, integrating technologies and architectural designs that prioritize residents' control over their personal data while maintaining essential safety measures. This topic will intertwine urban planning advancements with ethical considerations, aiming for smart cities where residents are both protected and empowered within the digital landscape. Additionally, it will investigate how design choices can promote social cohesion and mental well-being by fostering environments that respect personal space and individuality.",
