                    "text": "Building on Sally's research on urban biodiversity, I propose the topic \"Designing Privacy-By-Design Cities: Weaving Individual Autonomy Into Smart Urban Spaces.\" This innovative concept would explore how future city planning can incorporate technological advancements and eco-friendly design elements to create an environment that prioritizes both privacy and autonomy, while also fostering mental well-being. By examining various urban planning strategies through a lens of individual freedom, this topic seeks to develop guidelines for integrating technologies into city infrastructure in a way that respects residents' rights without compromising safety or environmental sustainability. This proposal merges Sally's findings on the benefits of green spaces with my vision for privacy-centric smart cities, ultimately aiming to craft urban landscapes where citizens can thrive amidst digital connectivity and ecological harmony.",
