                    "text": "\"Technology-Enhanced Urban Biodiversity: Fostering Ecosystems within Future Smart Cities\" will explore the convergence of urban development and natural ecosystem integration using cutting-edge technology. The topic delves into how smart city initiatives can support biodiversity through green infrastructure, biophilic design principles, and digital monitoring tools that create harmonious living spaces for both humans and wildlife. By leveraging IoT sensors, AI analysis, and community engagement platforms, cities will not only become more resilient but also offer enriched experiences to residents by bringing nature back into the urban fabric while maintaining technological advancements at its core.",
